{
  "id": "COMPOUND:38271 - PROTEIN:5787",
  "verbalization": "Sasanquasaponin I appears to exert its biological effects through a shared target, Microtubule-associated protein 1B, which is targeted by multiple compounds, including 4-Fluorobenzoic acid, tridec-2-ynyl ester and Petroraspailyne B1. These compounds, in turn, target RXF 631, suggesting a potential mechanism of action involving the modulation of microtubule-associated proteins. The presence of multiple pathways converging on RXF 631 through different targets indicates a possible role for Microtubule-associated protein 1B in the regulation of RXF 631 activity. The consistent targeting of Microtubule-associated protein 1B by Sasanquasaponin I and other compounds suggests a plausible mechanism of action, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be elucidated. The evidence supports a potential relationship between Sasanquasaponin I and RXF 631, but further experimental validation is required to confirm the mechanistic link.",
